cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use these materials, please cite them using these metadata.
type: dataset
title: "Warrant study: tasks, harness and run records for an exploratory evaluation of evidence-gated acceptance of code written by an AI agent"
abstract: >-
  Twenty small Python command-line tasks with visible checks, hidden checks, audit
  suites, reference and deliberately broken implementations; the harness; a seeded-defect
  evaluation of 160 broken implementations; and 40 agent runs (Claude Code driving
  gpt-oss:20b) under visible-only acceptance and under Warrant's gate, with run records
  and analysis. Exploratory, not pre-registered; tasks written by AI agents and reviewed
  by an AI model.
authors:
  - given-names: Tiago
    family-names: Miranda de Leao
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0003-6386-5941"
    alias: mv2a
repository-code: https://github.com/mv2a/warrant-study
url: https://github.com/mv2a/warrant-study
license: Apache-2.0
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-09-30
keywords:
  - AI coding agents
  - hidden tests
  - test overfitting
  - acceptance gates
  - mutation testing
